From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] core: keep the certified ANS kexec handoff

Resetting the ANS host or its translations destroys the state required
by the next kernel. Retain the stopped-DMA handoff only where the device
tree requests it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/kexec_core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/kexec_core.c b/kernel/kexec_core.c
index dc770b9a6..819650bcd 100644
--- a/kernel/kexec_core.c
+++ b/kernel/kexec_core.c
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ atomic_t __kexec_lock = ATOMIC_INIT(0);
 
 /* Flag to indicate we are going to kexec a new kernel */
 bool kexec_in_progress = false;
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kexec_in_progress);
 
 bool kexec_file_dbg_print;
 
